Recover the DBM<>APM correlation comment (e.g. a sqlcommenter-style ``/*dddbs=...*/`` tag) for non stored-procedure statements in Query Activity. Previously, SQL Server's own ``statement_start_offset``/``statement_end_offset`` excluded any comment preceding a statement from ``statement_text``, and the check only recovered it from the full batch text when the statement had stored-procedure context, silently breaking the ``Calling Service`` correlation panel for ordinary statements.
